# Per-example pipeline configuration for the "traefik-golang" awesome-compose
# example. Only "backend" is built/minimized. "frontend" (traefik:2.6) is a
# vendor image, unchanged, and requires mounting /var/run/docker.sock into the
# container for its Docker-provider service discovery to work — a
# security-sensitive operation we deliberately avoid for a test harness.
# Deliberate scope decision: test "backend" directly on its own port (80),
# skipping the traefik routing layer entirely. `backend` has no depends_on, so
# leaving COMPOSE_DEPS unset keeps `frontend` (and the socket mount) out of
# every compose invocation. Documented in original/functional-baseline.md.
EXAMPLE=traefik-golang
COMPOSE_FILE=vendor/awesome-compose/traefik-golang/compose.yaml
COMPOSE_SERVICE=backend
IMAGE_NAME=dip-traefik-golang
CONTAINER_PORT=80
HOST_PORT=8088
HEALTH_PATH=/
HEALTH_EXPECT="Hello from Docker"
